xt":"Make the pickles: stir the vinegar, sugar and salt with {qty 1/4 cup} warm water until dissolved. Add the carrot and daikon and leave for at least {time 20 min} while you cook.","uses":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"text":"Toss the tofu slabs gently in the cornstarch. Heat the oil in the skillet over medium-high heat and fry the tofu until golden and crisp, {time 3-4 min} per side.","uses":[5,6,7]},{"text":"Mix the soy sauce, maple syrup and garlic, pour it over the tofu and toss for {time 30 sec} until the glaze turns sticky. Take the pan off the heat.","uses":[8,9,10]},{"text":"Stir the mayonnaise and sriracha together. Split the rolls, warm them in the oven for a few minutes if you like, and spread the insides with the spicy mayo.","uses":[11,12,13]},{"text":"Fill each roll with tofu, drained pickles, cucumber, cilantro and jalapeño.","uses":[14,15,16]}]}